mode: "100644"
text: "# Instagram SEO 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (IG search + ranking signals move).*\n\n## The POV: Instagram is now a keyword search engine — keywords replaced hashtags\nSince **late 2024** (official in **2026**), Instagram shifted from **hashtag-based discovery to keyword-based\nsearch** — the biggest discovery change since Reels. **Hashtags are deprioritized to 3–5** (still clickable\n**topic labels**, no longer the discovery driver). **A large and growing share of discovery and new followers\nnow starts from search**, not the feed (no reliable public share figure — never quote one); Gen Z/Millennials\noften search IG instead of Google. IG search is a **closed system** (pulls\nfrom within the app — usernames, bios, captions, hashtags, locations; **no external crawl, no backlinks**),\n**but Google + Bing now index IG captions** (esp. professional accounts), so content can surface externally +\nin AI answers.\n\n## How IG search works (≈3 steps)\n1. **Semantic analysis** — breaks down the searcher's intent.\n2. **Metadata matching** — scans the **Name field, bio, and captions** for a **keyword cluster** (a group of\n   3–5 related terms proving topical authority).\n3. **Visual recognition** — **Computer Vision** \"sees\" the pixels/objects and checks **alt text**; if the\n   visual doesn't **match** the caption, ranking drops. **Search = keyword-driven; Explore = behavior-driven**\n   (optimize each differently).\n\n## Where keywords go (the IG surfaces)\n- **Name field (display name):** a high-weight search label — include the niche (\"Jane Smith | Austin\n  Realtor\"). **Handle:** keyword-relevant (@london.coffee.reviews > @coffeeislife44). **Bio:** indexable (IG +\n  Google) — niche + offer + location + a keyword + CTA.\n- **Captions:** searchable/indexed — **write for search first.** **Primary keyword in the first sentence /\n  first ~125 chars** (the visible preview); natural long-tail matching real queries (\"Easy vegan dinner in 10\n  minutes\" beats a context-free clever hook); longer captions (150–300 words) help. **3–5 hashtags** as\n  labels.\n- **Alt text:** classifies the visual + must **match** the caption (Computer Vision). **On-screen Reel text:**\n  transcribed + indexed. **Reel audio:** transcribed — say the **primary keyword in the first 3 seconds.**\n  **Auto-captions:** a meaningful watch-time lift (most viewers watch sound-off) **and** indexed (two-for-one). **Category + location** (a professional\n  account unlocks both).\n\n## Ranking + behaviour\n- **Engagement quality:** **saves, shares, watch time, replays > likes**; Reels live on **completion rate +\n  shares + trending audio.** Engagement creates a discovery flywheel.\n- **Reels deprioritized** for visible **other-platform watermarks** (remove the TikTok watermark) or low-res.\n- **The \"Raw Content Revolution\" (2026):** IG prioritizes **authentic, human-made** content and rewards\n  **retention + sends** — AI reads your keywords, but a human voice earns the engagement.\n\n## Research method + timeline\n- **Research:** scan the **captions + on-screen text of top-ranking Reels** for recurring phrases; check\n  competitors' **Name fields**; use **Google \"People Also Ask\"** (since Google indexes IG). Build a 3–5 term\n  **cluster.** *Never fabricate volume.*\n- **Timeline (slow burn):** profile-visits-from-search lift in **2–4 weeks**; non-follower reach **30–60\n  days**; full compounding **90–120 days** — then posts keep gaining views/saves for months. **No keyword\n  stuffing** (suppressed + spammy); **no irrelevant hashtags** (#follow4follow hurts credibility).\n"
